15 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a line graph of body weight over time in three groups treated with vehicle, SDX-7320 2.0 mg/kg, and SDX-7320 6.0 mg/kg, with significant weight reduction in the high-dose group. Panel B presents a line graph of food consumption per body weight over four weeks, showing similar trends across groups. Panel C displays a scatter plot of epididymal adipose mass, with the high-dose group showing significant reduction. Panel D shows retroperitoneal adipose mass, with reduction for both treatment groups, most pronounced in the high dose. Panel E presents inguinal adipose mass, again with a significant decrease for the high-dose group. Panel F is a scatter plot of leptin levels, reduced in the high-dose group. Panel G features adiponectin levels, with a statistically significant increase only in the high-dose group. Panel H shows the leptin/adiponectin ratio, significantly reduced in the high-dose group. Each panel compares vehicle, low-dose, and high-dose treatment using dots and statistical annotations.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a line graph comparing body weight change over seventy days for six groups of rats treated with vehicle, SDX-7320 at three dosages, or SDX-7539 at two dosages. Panel B shows a semi-logarithmic plot of plasma SDX-7539 concentrations over twenty-four hours after dosing, with different curves for each group. Panel C SDX-7539 Cmax comparing percent body weight change versus SDX-7539 maximum concentration for SDX-7320 and SDX-7539 groups. Panel D depicts percent body weight change versus SDX-7539 area under the curve for SDX-7320 and SDX-7539 groups. Error bars indicate standard error of the mean throughout.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Eight-panel scientific figure with line and dot plots comparing tumor volume, body weight, and adipose tissue mass in obese and lean groups with or without SDX-7320 treatment. Panels A, B, and D show tumor volume over time; panels C and E show body weight over time; panels F, G, and H show endpoint measurements of epididymal, retroperitoneal, and inguinal adipose mass. Distinct colored lines and symbols represent different groups and doses, with statistical significance indicated by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a line graph comparing tumor volume over time between obese and lean vehicle-treated groups, with obese mice showing higher tumor growth. Panel B is a line graph showing tumor volume in obese vehicle and obese SDX-7320-treated groups, with SDX-7320 markedly reducing tumor growth. Panel C illustrates body weight over time in obese vehicle versus obese SDX-7320 groups, indicating a slight weight decrease with treatment. Panel D compares tumor volume between lean vehicle and lean SDX-7320-treated groups, with lower tumor growth in treated mice. Panel E displays body weight in lean vehicle versus lean SDX-7320 groups, showing minimal changes in body weight with treatment. Error bars represent standard error of the mean, and asterisks denote statistical significance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a Venn diagram comparing up-regulated genes between obese and lean groups treated with SDX versus vehicle, with 453 unique to obese, 4 unique to lean, and 10 overlapping. Panel B presents a Venn diagram of down-regulated genes, showing 58 unique to obese, 8 to lean, and 3 shared. Panel C and D display bar charts of hallmark pathway enrichment scores from gene set enrichment analysis for obese and lean groups, respectively. Panels E and F present dot plots of RPM values for Gzm gene expression across treatment groups in obese and lean mice. Panel G shows a dot plot of Perforin1 expression across all groups, and panel H shows a dot plot for CD206/MRC1 expression, highlighting significant differences between treatment groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Ten-panel scientific figure showing line and scatter plots comparing effects of SDX-7320, vehicle, and tirzepatide treatments in mice. Panel A shows tumor volume over time, Panel B depicts body weight over time, Panels C-E illustrate mass of various adipose tissues, Panels F-H display serum biomarker levels and Panels I-J display the results of plasma metabolomics analysis. Statistical significance is denoted by asterisks, with colored circles representing individual data points for each group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
